Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.35,0:00:03.59,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}We introduce GEM, a geometric episodic memory
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.59,0:00:05.60,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}that uses a streaming geometry model
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.60,0:00:07.51,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}to help existing navigation policies
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.51,0:00:10.85,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}return to previously observed places without retraining.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.46,0:00:15.44,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}We first show how this memory supports an indoor revisit,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.44,0:00:19.22,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}where the robot must return to a place shown in a goal image.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.22,0:00:21.68,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}Both runs share the same starting pose,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.68,0:00:24.08,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}goal image, and survey history,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.08,0:00:26.77,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}but the baseline stops before a glass wall,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.77,0:00:30.45,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}while GEM uses that history to reach the destination.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.45,0:00:36.22,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}In the outdoor trial, GEM turns toward the remembered goal
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.22,0:00:39.13,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}and updates its direction as the robot moves,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.13,0:00:43.22,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}while the unchanged NavDP controller plans the local motion.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.22,0:00:45.46,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}Across ten real-world settings,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.46,0:00:48.73,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}GEM reaches the goal in 25/30 trials,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.73,0:00:51.41,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}compared with 4/30 for the baseline.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.29,0:01:00.85,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}We also evaluate in Habitat on HM3D and MP3D.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.46,0:01:05.68,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}In this episode, both methods first reach two novel goals,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.68,0:01:08.03,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}collecting observations that remain available
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.03,0:01:11.93,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}when the third goal asks them to revisit an earlier location.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.93,0:01:13.89,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}GEM uses this accumulated history
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.89,0:01:16.75,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}to locate the goal relative to the current camera,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.75,0:01:20.19,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}allowing it to complete the sequence while the baseline fails.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.31,0:01:25.16,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}These revisits rely on shared geometry,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.16,0:01:28.37,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}which a frozen model builds by estimating pose and depth
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.37,0:01:32.00,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}from RGB images, without external pose measurements.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.45,0:01:35.48,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}This memory combines a working state for streaming geometry
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.48,0:01:38.74,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}with an archive that links past images to their geometry,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.74,0:01:42.10,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}and both are retained as the robot moves between goals.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.50,0:01:44.40,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}When a new goal image is given,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.40,0:01:46.98,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}GEM matches it to a supporting historical view
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.98,0:01:51.35,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}and uses archived depth to estimate and verify the goal pose.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.35,0:01:53.84,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}The shared geometry then connects that pose
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.84,0:01:57.45,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}to the current camera, even without direct image overlap.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.40,0:02:01.26,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}Once the goal pose is cached,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.26,0:02:04.23,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}GEM updates its bearing as the robot moves.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.23,0:02:08.03,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}NavDP receives this cue alongside the original goal image,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.03,0:02:11.43,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}while ViNT and NoMaD use the verified historical view;
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.43,0:02:14.70,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}if verification fails, the original inputs are retained.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.34,0:02:17.51,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}To test these benefits across controllers,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.51,0:02:21.51,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}we compare three frozen policies on HM3D and MP3D
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.51,0:02:24.81,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}under matched histories and evaluation conditions.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.81,0:02:27.11,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}Adding GEM improves revisit success
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.11,0:02:29.98,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}by 60.7 to 81.0 percentage points,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.98,0:02:32.86,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}while success on novel goals is maintained or improved
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.86,0:02:34.70,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}across all six comparisons.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.29,0:02:38.56,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}When we extend the evaluation to continuous navigation,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.56,0:02:41.71,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}where each method builds its own history across goals,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.71,0:02:44.71,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}GEM completes 64 three-goal sequences,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.71,0:02:46.70,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}compared with 12 for the baseline.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.25,0:02:50.57,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}When both methods receive the same two-goal histories,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.57,0:02:52.28,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}third-goal revisit success rises
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.28,0:02:54.32,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}from eight to seventeen out of twenty,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.32,0:02:57.55,Narration,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,1052)}while novel success remains 4/20 for both.
